\pard\s2 5.2\tab Primary Complete-Document Performance\par

\pard\s0 Under the primary complete_unmasked condition, all three methods correctly classified all 99 test documents. Accuracy, macro precision, macro recall, and macro F1 were therefore 1.0000 for BERT, plain Gemini, and Gemini+RAG. The corresponding confusion matrices were fully diagonal, with no misclassification for any of the four agencies. This result shows that each architecture was capable of routing complete documents from unseen document families when all original textual evidence was available. However, the perfect score should be interpreted as a ceiling result for this specific test set, not as proof of perfect performance on future government documents.\par

\pard\s4 Table 4. Performance on the primary complete_unmasked condition (99 documents per method).\par
