\pard\s2 5.3\tab Robustness Across Registered Text Conditions\par

\pard\s0 The robustness conditions produced the clearest difference among the methods. Plain Gemini and Gemini+RAG achieved a macro F1 of 1.0000 under all ten conditions, including partial-document inputs and versions in which explicit agency names, form numbers, government URLs, and related identifiers were masked. BERT achieved 1.0000 in five conditions and remained above 0.95 in every condition, but its performance declined when some textual evidence was removed. Its lowest macro F1 was 0.9587 for beginning-only unmasked text. The other non-perfect BERT scores were 0.9910 for end-only unmasked, 0.9664 for complete masked, 0.9664 for beginning-only masked, and 0.9842 for end-only masked. These results indicate that BERT was highly accurate but more sensitive than the LLM approaches to where evidence appeared and to the removal of explicit identifiers.\par

